								<wikidot:authorUserId>1316614</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>To be clear, we already have a J explaining redactions, a series article explaining over-redactions, and three different J's explaining overpowered self-inserts. There's also the pile of horsecrap SCP to explain generally bad items, and the 1234-J poking fun at the format itself. This doesn't really add anything to our literature on the subject of subpar articles and annoying users.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
